eye-care awareness"},{"text":"Retina and glaucoma clinic exposure"},{"text":"Ophthalmic surgery workflow awareness"},{"text":"Digital ophthalmology knowledge"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an Ophthalmic Clinical Portfolio containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ophthalmology internship record"},{"text":"Vision-screening experience"},{"text":"Ophthalmic equipment training"},{"text":"Diagnostic-testing exposure"},{"text":"Cataract-care case study"},{"text":"Glaucoma-screening case study"},{"text":"Retinal-screening project"},{"text":"Pediatric eye-care project"},{"text":"Digital ophthalmology project"},{"text":"Relevant clinical certifications"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"“Eye-care professional with strong ophthalmic clinical-support, patient-assessment, diagnostic-equipment, documentation, and digital eye-care skills.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest combination for this career is patient care + ophthalmic technology + diagnostic support + clinical communication + digital ophthalmology. This provides a practical foundation for progressing from an Eye Care Assistant into ophthalmic technology, specialized diagnostic services, pediatric eye care, retinal/glaucoma services, or technology-enabled eye-care roles."}]}]}